<!DOCTYPE node PUBLIC "-//freedesktop//DTD D-BUS Object Introspection 1.0//EN"
 "http://www.freedesktop.org/standards/dbus/1.0/introspect.dtd">
<!--
  org.unifiedpush.Distributor2, as the UnifiedPush D-Bus specification 0.3.0 defines it
  (https://unifiedpush.org/developers/spec/dbus/), at /org/unifiedpush/Distributor on
  org.unifiedpush.Distributor.vibeos.

  Register options: "service" s (the app's D-Bus name, which the caller must own), "token" s (the app's secret for
  this registration, 1 to 100 bytes), "description" s (up to 100 bytes, shown in Settings), "vapid" s (the app
  server's VAPID public key: an uncompressed P-256 point in base64url, 87 characters).
  Result: "success" s, REGISTRATION_SUCCEEDED or REGISTRATION_FAILED, and with a failure "reason" s:
    UNAUTHORIZED     the caller does not own "service", or the token is another app's
    ACTION_REQUIRED  the app has 16 registrations, or there are 256 in all
  An option that breaks the spec's rules gets the error org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InvalidArgs.
  On success the app's org.unifiedpush.Connector2.NewEndpoint follows: at once when the push server has subscribed
  the topic, otherwise once it has (it refuses messages for a topic that never had a subscriber).

  Unregister options: "token" s. An unknown token is ignored. Unregistered confirms it to the app.
-->
<node>
  <interface name="org.unifiedpush.Distributor2">
    <method name="Register">
      <arg name="options" type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="result" type="a{sv}" direction="out"/>
    </method>
    <method name="Unregister">
      <arg name="options" type="a{sv}" direction="in"/>
      <arg name="result" type="a{sv}" direction="out"/>
    </method>
  </interface>
</node>
